{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01D5aJnGvbnErMqVohKZswSZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **`answers/05-004-prevent-factual-errors-in-summarization.md`** — Q4: Prevent factual errors in summarization.\n\n**Key content:**\n- **Framing:** Probes whether the candidate understands extrinsic hallucination (model adds facts from training data) vs intrinsic hallucination (model contradicts source due to attention drift) — and has layered mitigations beyond \"just lower the temperature.\"\n- **Three-layer defence stack:**\n  1. **Prompt layer** — closed-world grounding instruction + `temperature=0`\n  2. **Chunking strategy** — Map-Reduce for long docs (summarize each 512–1024 token chunk independently then reduce); prevents \"lost in the middle\" attention drift\n  3. **Post-generation faithfulness gate** — async RAGAS faithfulness (LLM-as-judge) for throughput; DeBERTa NLI entailment for regulated domains\n- **Concrete example:** Financial earnings-call summarizer — Map-Reduce with GPT-4o-mini vs full-context GPT-4o reduced intrinsic error rate from 8% → 1.8% at 70% lower cost\n- **Three pitfalls:** T=0 as magic bullet, RAGAS sync blocking, BLEU/ROUGE as accuracy proxies\n- **Cross-links:** Q3 (general hallucination stack), Q5 (medical chatbot variant), Q9 (n-gram metric pitfalls)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339,"cache_read_input_tokens":66565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":339,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2e76bdb-4526-41de-8358-5ce2510dafd1","uuid":"62bc3143-f102-4b93-82df-7ab4d70e934f"}
